{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And the days of Israel drew near to die</b> — Its solution: as the days of Israel drew near to die, he called for his son Joseph, and this was in the final year of his life. Its meaning is that he perceived in himself the ebbing of his strength and the increase of weakness, yet he was not sick; rather, he knew that he would not live long, and therefore he called for his son Joseph. And after Joseph returned to Egypt, he fell ill, and it was told to Joseph, and he came to him with his two sons so that he might bless them. And similarly, <b>\"and the days of David drew near to die\"</b> (I Kings 2:1), and there (verse 2) it is said, <b>\"I am going the way of all the earth,\"</b> for he knew in himself likewise."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:46:18.904777642Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}